# The tools for agencies (tests/t1/museum_editor_tools.sh), on the project of the table session (golden/museum-editor/table.json) in a folder
# with its photograph. What the menu bar, the context menus and the system do is in session.system; the gaps left here are the frames in
# which each of its events may arrive.
# The storyboard: every sequence selected; aligned at the top and spread across from the menu bar (frames 5 to 12); then nudged down,
# copied, pasted (the three copies are selected), nudged right by five steps.
4 key a meta
14 key ArrowDown
16 key c meta
18 key v meta
20 key ArrowRight shift
# The context menu of the first sequence: "Open its table". There, both media selected; aligned left from the menu bar (frames 32 to 64).
24 move 350 200
25 right-down
26 right-up
30 key a meta
# Nudged, duplicated; the two copies are aligned at the top from the menu bar (frames 72 to 144).
66 key ArrowRight
67 key ArrowDown shift
69 key d meta
# The copies are cut. The context menu of the sequence beside the first one opens its table, where the two media are pasted.
146 key x meta
148 key Escape
151 move 600 182
152 right-down
153 right-up
157 key v meta
# Nothing selected; the context menu of the table: "Select all"; the two media are centred vertically from the menu bar, then a picture
# is dropped on the window from outside the project (frames 170 to 342): it is copied into the project folder and the question of
# "Add a file" opens on it.
159 key Escape
161 move 800 300
162 right-down
163 right-up
